  "title": "India's E-Visa Expansion and New Ports",
  "summary": "The Ministry of Home Affairs has announced the expansion of India's e-visa entry network to include 11 international ports and 9 land ports, including the newly added land port Attari on the India-Pakistan border. This enhances access to Indian ports and airports for international travelers.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "India expanded its e-visa entry network to 88 ports, including 37 airports and 38 seaports.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The new land ports include Darranga, Gede, Ghojadanga, Haridaspur, Jaigaon, Dawki, Moreh, and Attari.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "International travelers with a Pakistani passport or of Pakistani origin must apply for a regular visa at an Indian Mission.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
